# Third-party components and their licenses

PyDownloader ships the FFmpeg binary and uses third-party libraries. The list
below is compiled as dependencies are added; the full license text is shipped
with the installer in the `{app}\licenses` folder.

| Component | License | Source |
|---|---|---|
| FFmpeg (`ffmpeg.exe`) | GPLv2+/LGPL2.1+ (BtbN/gyan.dev build, GPL version 2) | https://ffmpeg.org , https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds |
| PySide6 (Qt 6) | LGPLv3 (Qt LGPL license agreement) | https://www.qt.io/qt-licensing |
| Playwright for Python | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-python |
| Chromium (fallback, downloaded on demand) | BSD-3 (Chromium project) | https://www.chromium.org |
| uBlock Origin Lite (`uBlock.crx`, distributed unmodified) | GPLv3 | https://github.com/uBlockOrigin/uBOL-home |
| httpx | BSD-3 | https://github.com/encode/httpx |
| cryptography | Apache-2.0/BSD | https://github.com/pyca/cryptography |
| lxml | BSD-2 | https://lxml.de |
| imageio-ffmpeg | BSD-2 | https://github.com/imageio/imageio-ffmpeg |
| packaging | MIT/Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/pypa/packaging |
| Inno Setup (build tool) | libpriyut / GNU GPL, freely used to build the installer | https://www.innosetup.com |

Notes:
- FFmpeg is invoked as a separate process (`subprocess`); the application does
  not link its libraries; in the installer FFmpeg ships as a separate binary in
  `{app}\bin`.
- DRM content (Widevine/PlayReady/FairPlay) is not processed by the
  application: such streams are skipped, protection bypass is not performed.
- At build time the version of each library is pinned in `requirements.txt`.
